      "box": [
        72.0,
        208.0520477294922,
        128.062255859375,
        227.55343627929688
      ],
      "text": "WOMAN:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        228.1547088623047,
        514.851806640625,
        286.6736145019531
      ],
      "text": "Well there was that study which showed that primary age children generated\nmore ideas when they were writing by hand than using a keyboard. I would\nhave guessed that would be the case.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        299.6110534667969,
        105.86299896240234,
        319.1124572753906
      ],
      "text": "MAN:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        319.59368896484375,
        494.20654296875,
        378.2336120605469
      ],
      "text": "Hmm yeah I never associated spatial awareness with handwriting either. I\nthought spatial awareness was more to do with knowing where you are in\nrelation to objects or other people.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        391.0520324707031,
        128.062255859375,
        410.5534362792969
      ],
      "text": "WOMAN:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        411.0346984863281,
        516.7401733398438,
        469.6736145019531
      ],
      "text": "I thought that too. But good spatial awareness is essential for writing because\nyou have to space words correctly. It’s not just fine motor skills that improve\nthrough writing, as I’d always assumed.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        482.4920349121094,
        105.86299896240234,
        501.9934387207031
      ],
      "text": "MAN:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        502.5936584472656,
        523.169677734375,
        600.8336181640625
      ],
      "text": "Handwriting is so much harder for children with dyspraxia, who have problems\ncoordinating movement. It’s good there are lots of things you can do in the\nclassroom to help them. They need so much more support with letter\nformation. You need to play lots of games to help them distinguish letter\nshapes. It takes a lot of patience.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        613.6520385742188,
        128.062255859375,
        633.1534423828125
      ],
      "text": "WOMAN:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        633.7537231445312,
        507.80389404296875,
        672.4736328125
      ],
      "text": "Yeah, I like the idea of using one of those pens that lights up if you press too\nhard. That seems like a really simple solution.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        685.2920532226562,
        105.86299896240234,
        704.79345703125
      ],
      "text": "MAN:\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        705.3937377929688,
        513.3330688476562,
        763.9136352539062
      ],
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. I’m not sure there’s much you can do about children with\ndyspraxia writing very slowly. It’s more important to focus on accuracy and as\nthey get more confident, I think they eventually speed up.\n"
    }
  ]
